    "cv_r2_specified": 0.533,
    "cv_r2_with_xg_chain_added_back": 0.8921,
    "cv_r2_without_chain_and_buildup": 0.5363,
    "r2_inflation_from_xg_chain": 0.3591
  },
  "caveat": "This regression is not a measurement of finishing ability and its headline R squared is not evidence that it is a good model. Understat's xGChain includes the expected goals of possessions the player finished himself and xGBuildup excludes shots and key passes, so the difference between the two columns contains the target almost by construction. See the leakage block for the correlation and for the ablation R squared with xGChain removed. The specified leaderboard ranks players whose own shots are an unusual share of the possessions they touch. The leak-free leaderboard ranks players whose shot volume is unusual given a model that leaves roughly half the variance unexplained, which is still ample room for team attacking volume, penalty box occupancy and single season noise on 450 to 3000 minutes. Read neither as a ranking of talent.",
  "caveat_with_value": "Cross validated R squared on the specified feature set is 0.533. xGChain is excluded from that feature set because Understat credits it for possessions the player finished himself: its difference from xGBuildup correlates with npxG per 90 at 0.904, and a model that includes it reaches 0.892 by reconstructing the target rather than predicting it. With the leak removed the fit still leaves roughly half the variance unexplained, so the leaderboard does not measure finishing ability.",
